#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065063} :activity/id #uuid "6a8803f8-cdad-59a2-a9d6-fe10c0d001fc" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048403 :topic/id #uuid "9c41899e-334d-5c90-83f2-ff0d4e02a917" :topic/math-academy-id 316} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065063 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065432 :tutorial/content "At first sight, the integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int x \\sqrt{x+2} \\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nmight not seem like it can be solved using substitution because $x$ is not the derivative of $x+2.$ But in fact, with some clever manipulation, we can indeed solve it using substitution!\n\nSetting\n\n$$\nu=x+2,\n$$\n\nand computing the required derivatives gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int x \\sqrt{x+2} \\,\\textrm{d}x=\\int x \\sqrt{u} \\,\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nSo we still have an $x$ in our integrand. However, we can get rid of it by solving for $x$ in the rule $u=x+2.$ We get\n\n$$\nx=u-2,\n$$\n\nand using this, the integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u= & \\int (u-2)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int (u-2){u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral by multiplying out the product and integrating the resulting function with respect to $u\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (u-2){u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\int ({u}^{3/2}-2{u}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u-2\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{4}{3}{u}^{3/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the final step, we substitute $u=x+2,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{5}(x+2)^{5/2}-\\frac{4}{3}(x+2)^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x+2)^{5}}-\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{(x+2)^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "6d16cf43-c7f8-5600-82a2-55a301cc5a4f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 843 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "cdacec4c-760a-523e-bd19-189115482c57" :step/math-academy-id 1626 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065065}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065064 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064209 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064080 :question/id #uuid "109a6d6e-8e62-5eac-bfa8-7c059399efe8" :question/math-academy-id "e-457"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94ad8efa-33ee-5451-b6b9-c99cb81a9ba2" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048332}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064493} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064497} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284633} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319095} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319096} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319239} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319242} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319244} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332733} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332734} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392689} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528003}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Definite Integrals of Algebraic Functions Using Substitution"} :step/id #uuid "04eb5284-3202-50f0-b91f-023a0a6f28a8" :step/math-academy-id 1627} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065065 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064210 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064081 :question/id #uuid "a40f6e7e-f4d3-5f3e-bf9d-99c640e36274" :question/math-academy-id "e-458"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2feb2115-bd75-5c09-87cc-f10cf46c182f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050771}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064752} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064860} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247408} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259761} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292607} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292610} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292611} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323705} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323708} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332707} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332708} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332732}] :knowledge-point/title "Calcula